## 2. DDoS Danger: Unbounded Thread Spawning (Task.WhenAll)
In AggregatedFeed.cs, the feed mapping logic loops through every item and fires network tasks simultaneously using an unthrottled Task.WhenAll:

foreach (var reference in references) {
    var task = reference.GetResultAsync(feedItem.Title.Text);
    tasks.Add(task);
}var results = await Task.WhenAll(tasks);


* The Failure Vector: If your source XML feed has 50 items and you have 3 references configured, your code will instantly burst 150 simultaneous outbound HTTP requests to Rotten Tomatoes and Metacritic. Those servers will detect this as a Distributed Denial of Service (DDoS) attack or an aggressive scraper and immediately IP-ban your production server.
* The Fix: Throttling is mandatory. Implement a local SemaphoreSlim(3, 3) inside your fetching service to ensure that only a small, safe number of concurrent requests are processed at any given moment.

